<title>USA: Louisville feeder cattle prices up $1-$6 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Louisville feeder cattle prices up $1-$6 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>LOUISVILLE 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cattle and Calves Receipts - 1,200. Compared to last week's close, feeder steers were $2.00 to $4.00 per cwt higher, instances $5.00 to $6.00 on 250-350 lb calves. Feeder heifers $1.00 to $3.00 higher.</p>
<p>Feeder Steers - Medium and Large 1 500-600 lbs 82.00-89.50; 600-700 lbs 80.00-86.20; 700-800 lbs few 75.00-81.50. Small 1 400-500 lbs 75.00-80.00. Medium and Large 2 300-400 lbs 83.00-90.00; 400-500 lbs 76.00-85.00; pkg 585 lbs 74.25; 600-700 lbs 67.25-76.00. Holsteins - Large 2 23 head 807 lbs 65.25; 20 head 908 lbs 63.70.</p>
<p>Feeder Heifers - Medium and Large 1 500-600 lbs few 76.00-79.50, fleshy 68.50-73.00; 600-700 lbs few 67.00-70.50; 800-90 lbs 63.50-64.75. Small 1 500- 600 lbs 64.50-73.00; 600-700 lbs 61.50-68.00.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
